      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "We have been sold a false narrative where ownership is merely a subscription to constant upgrades and service fees. Continuing to dictate how long our property lasts betrays a fundamental social contract: that when we buy something, we own it. The Right to Repair isn't just about saving money; it's about reclaiming autonomy in a world increasingly dictated by proprietary black boxes. It is time we demand genuine stewardship over the technology we use every single day.",
      "source": "target",
